  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> for a boy, add both parents&rsquo; heights, add 5&nbsp;in (13&nbsp;cm) and divide by 2; for a girl, subtract 5&nbsp;in and divide by 2. About 95% of children end up within <strong>3.3&nbsp;in (8.5&nbsp;cm)</strong> of this. The calculator also uses the child&rsquo;s current growth percentile for a sharper estimate.</p></div>

